WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.134 line:0%
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)
-And finally...

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:05.471 line:0%
New Rule, if you want to know
why your kids are so bratty,

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:08.274 line:0%
entitled, and always asking
for your credit card,

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:10.710 line:0%
check their Spotify playlists.
(SMACKS LIPS)

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:13.512 line:0%
Because the messages
they're hearing are a full 180

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.115 line:0%
from what kids used to hear
when they turned on the radio.

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:18.150
Sinéad O'Connor
will be in the mo--

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.753
In Memoriam reel
at the Grammys this Sunday,

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:22.956
and it would be great
if they quoted what she said

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.324
when she once pulled out
of the show in protest.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.459
She said...

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:37.837
How about this year
for a new Grammy category?

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:41.273
"Best Song Where No One Brags
About Buying a Lot of Shit."

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:45.645
(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.449
And before 1990,

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:54.020
there were like two songs ever
that glorified money.

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:58.758
-"Money (That's What I Want)."
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.459
And "Material Girl."

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:05.664
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:06.800
Well, uh,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.036
here's a short sampling
of some more recent offerings.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:17.043
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.082
And that's just the ones
that have "Money" in the title.

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:25.284
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:26.619
Why does this matter?

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:29.422
Because nothing molds
teenage hearts and minds

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:33.259
like music and music culture.
This is true across generations.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.861
When you turn 12,
you're done with your parents,

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.030
and start getting raised
by pop stars.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.132
-You--
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:46.238
(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:48.575
The older people
have the money and the power,

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.376
but kids rule the charts.

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:52.345
And the lyrics of your youth

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.613
are burned into your brain
like that time

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.716
you saw your father
getting out of the shower.

00:01:56.882 --> 00:02:02.522
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.857
I don't remembe-- (CHUCKLES)

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:06.692
I don't remember a lot
from eighth grade.

00:02:06.825 --> 00:02:08.327
Don't-- don't get me
on the formula

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.796
for the radius of a circle,

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.131
but if you ask me
to finish the lyric,

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.499
all you need is,

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:15.701
I'm pretty sure
I could come up with "Love."

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.604
But if I asked a kid today
to finish that lyric,

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:20.106
what would they say?

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:23.442
I'm not sure, but I know
what their heroes say.

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:24.777
They say things like...

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:34.120
And sure, it started in rap,
but everybody does it now...

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:39.392
Even country music
has songs like...

00:02:41.226 --> 00:02:45.632
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-Really?

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.637
(CLEARS THROAT)
The band Florida Georgia Line

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.207
has one about
how pimpy their truck is.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.409
-(SMACKS LIPS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:59.212
I don't know, but maybe
this kind of unbridled lusting

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.615
for material things
is actually the kind of grooming

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.450
parents should be worried about.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.853
We went from, so...

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.558
To...

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:18.998
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.736
Kids blame my generation
for ruining the planet,

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.238
but good luck saving it, kids,

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.940
if this is what
you're always dreaming about.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:31.410
Always hearing a drumbeat
that happiness results

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.012
from getting things,

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:35.515
things that a vast majority
don't have.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:39.251
The pop stars of my youth,
their message to me was

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:43.089
that what made them happy
was available to me too.

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:47.026
♪<i> Even though
 We ain't got money</i> ♪

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:50.662
♪<i> I'm so in love
 With you, honey...</i> ♪

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:53.499
(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:55.835
BILL MAHER: Yeah.

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.250
The Monkees sang...

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.358
Kanye says...

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:26.699
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:33.806
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:39.412
To which the Monkees said,

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.280
"It was more
of a rhetorical question."

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:45.217
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:46.386
John Lennon said...

00:04:48.887 --> 00:04:52.191
And 10,000 rappers said
we can't and we don't want to.

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:55.061
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-And you know what?

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.266
You know what?
I don't blame 'em.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:01.834
I get where this comes from.

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:03.569
There is a racial element
to this.

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:05.370
Suburban White hippie kids

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:08.440
had the luxury
of being anti-materialistic

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:09.775
because they were never denied

00:05:09.908 --> 00:05:11.677
material things
in the first place.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:14.179
There's a reason Jimmy Buffett
didn't sing about bling,

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:16.748
he was already eating
a cheeseburger in Paradise.

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:21.721
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:26.759
But the history
of Black people in America

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.794
is the history
of being denied the means,

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:30.930
and often even the right
to buy stuff,

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.097
including a home

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:34.066
in the neighborhood
you might want to live in.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.202
So, when the long denied
finally becomes available,

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:39.037
there's going
to be some flaunting.

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:40.740
If you were excluded
from luxury

00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:41.841
and then finally got it,

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:43.776
you wouldn't want
to shut up about it either.

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:45.744
But forever?

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:47.113
(AUDIENCE MEMBER LAUGHING)

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:49.615
And not just in rap,
everybody does it.

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:50.949 line:0%
♪<i> Versace...</i> ♪

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.351 line:0%
-♪<i> Fendi... ♪
 -♪ Jimmy Choo... ♪</i>

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:54.353 line:0%
-♪<i> Prada..</i> . ♪
-♪<i> Dolce Gabbana... ♪</i>

00:05:54.486 --> 00:05:55.821 line:0%
-♪<i> Louis Vuitton...</i> ♪
-♪<i> Gucci...</i> ♪

00:05:55.954 --> 00:05:57.423 line:0%
<i> -♪ Givenchy... ♪
 -♪ Chanel... ♪</i>

00:05:58.123 --> 00:05:59.792
-(SMACKS LIPS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:02.795
And if you-- and if your answer
to that is, "Okay, boomer."

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:06.499
-(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:08.601
That's-- that's not an answer.

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:11.237
And vomiting an inventory
of your possessions

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:12.504
doesn't make you a poet.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:16.609
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)
-And--

00:06:17.776 --> 00:06:22.781
And it's been done to death.

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:26.151
Aren't you tired of it?
I'm old, this shit is old.

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:31.724
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)
-Get--

00:06:33.225 --> 00:06:37.930
-Get a second idea for a song.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:45.338
Well... (CLEARS THROAT)
...actually, there is one,

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:46.538
"Sadness."

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.475
Hmm... (SMACKS LIPS)
...maybe they're connected.

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:53.045
Yeah, Spotify actually has data
on the types of songs

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:54.112
the kids like,

00:06:54.179 --> 00:06:56.081
and it shows that Gen Z's
number-one search

00:06:56.214 --> 00:06:57.917
last summer was, "Sad."

00:06:58.984 --> 00:07:00.920
Artists like Billie Eilish
and Demi Lovato

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:04.089
have pioneered a whole new genre
called, "Sad Bops."

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:05.591
A good beat,
you can dance to it,

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:06.925
and then you wanna
slit your throat.

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:09.928
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.964
I'm just saying
maybe they're connected.

00:07:14.132 --> 00:07:15.134
The good news is,

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:18.036
I've seen the music industry
clean up its act before.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.372
Not with sexual assault,
they're still doing that.

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:24.377
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-But--

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.979
But at least with the message
of the music,

00:07:27.112 --> 00:07:28.447
which for quite a long time

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:30.817
was dominated
with tearjerkers like...

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:36.222
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:07:38.657 --> 00:07:39.692
And...

00:07:42.227 --> 00:07:44.497
It was ugly, ugly,

00:07:44.697 --> 00:07:47.199
very sexist,
and very homophobic.

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:50.268
There was Ice-T and Ice Cube,
but no Ice Capades.

00:07:50.402 --> 00:07:55.241
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:07:57.877 --> 00:08:01.214
And we were okay with it,
until we weren't.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.915
And maybe it's time now?

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:05.083
It's not to be okay
with teaching kids

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:07.420
you're only as good
as how much stuff you have.

